IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc16-dna-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc16-open-court`

-- ccc16-tests-open-court.l4 -- tests for ccc16-open-court.l4 (sections 486 to 486.31, 486.7, 486.71).
-- Expected values were decided from the text (lines 8764-9012) before the run and are written beside each assertion.

`s 486 test: the prosecutor` MEANS `s 486 the prosecutor`
`s 486 test: a witness` MEANS `s 486 a witness`
`s 486 test: the court on its own motion` MEANS `s 486 the judge or justice on their own motion`
`s 486 test: the accused` MEANS `s 486 the accused`
`s 486 test: another person` MEANS `s 486 another person`
`s 486 test: the exclusion order` MEANS `s 486(1) the exclusion of all or any members of the public from the court room for all or part of the proceedings`
`s 486 test: the screen order` MEANS `s 486(1) that the witness testify behind a screen or other device that would allow the witness not to be seen by members of the public`

§ `s 486(1) -- open court, and the power to exclude`
#ASSERT `s 486(1) the proceedings against the accused are held in open court` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no order: "shall be held in open court"
#ASSERT `s 486(1) the proceedings against the accused are held in open court` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an order: the "but" clause, not covered
-- the power: the prosecutor, a witness or the judge or justice on their own motion; the opinion that the order is in the interest of public morals ... or is necessary to prevent injury to international relations ...
#ASSERT `s 486(1) the presiding judge or justice may order the exclusion of the public or that the witness testify behind a screen` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) (`s 486 test: the exclusion order`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486(1) the presiding judge or justice may order the exclusion of the public or that the witness testify behind a screen` (`s 486 test: a witness`) (`s 486 test: the screen order`) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- national security ground
#ASSERT `s 486(1) the presiding judge or justice may order the exclusion of the public or that the witness testify behind a screen` (`s 486 test: the court on its own motion`) (`s 486 test: the exclusion order`) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486(1) the presiding judge or justice may order the exclusion of the public or that the witness testify behind a screen` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) (`s 486 test: the exclusion order`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no opinion on either ground
#ASSERT `s 486(1) the presiding judge or justice may order the exclusion of the public or that the witness testify behind a screen` (`s 486 test: the accused`) (`s 486 test: the exclusion order`) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the accused is not among those the text names
#ASSERT `s 486(1) the presiding judge or justice may order the exclusion of the public or that the witness testify behind a screen` (`s 486 test: another person`) (`s 486 test: the exclusion order`) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486(1) the presiding judge or justice may order the exclusion of the public or that the witness testify behind a screen` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) (`s 486(1) an order of another kind`) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 486(1.1) -- where and when the application is made`
#ASSERT `s 486(1.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- during the proceedings, to the presiding judge or justice
#ASSERT `s 486(1.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- during the proceedings the text names only the presiding judge or justice
#ASSERT `s 486(1.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside
#ASSERT `s 486(1.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- that judge or justice has not been determined
#ASSERT `s 486(1.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the judge who will preside has not been determined: any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district
#ASSERT `s 486(1.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the judge who will preside has been determined: the grant is limited to that judge
#ASSERT `s 486(1.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- before the proceedings begin the text does not name the presiding judge
#ASSERT `s 486(1.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` `s 486(1.1) another judge or justice` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another judge

§ `s 486(2) -- factors`
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486(2)(a) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486(2)(b) the safeguarding of the interests of witnesses under the age of 18 years in all proceedings`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486(2)(c) the ability of the witness to give a full and candid account of the acts complained of if the order were not made`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486(2)(d) whether the witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486(2)(e) the protection of justice system participants who are involved in the proceedings`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486(2)(f) whether effective alternatives to the making of the proposed order are available in the circumstances`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (f) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486(2)(g) the salutary and deleterious effects of the proposed order`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (g) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486(2)(h) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (h): any other factor the judge or justice considers relevant
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486(2)(h) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (h): a factor the judge or justice does not consider relevant
#ASSERT `s 486(2) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486(2)(a) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- outside the determination the lead-in names

§ `s 486(3) -- reasons for not making an order`
#ASSERT `s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` (`Provision of the Code` OF 151, "") (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` (`Provision of the Code` OF 160, "(2)") (`s 486 test: the accused`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the accused may apply here
#ASSERT `s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` (`Provision of the Code` OF 160, "(3)") (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` (`Provision of the Code` OF 160, "(1)") (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- subsection 160(1) is not listed
#ASSERT `s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` (`Provision of the Code` OF 173, "(2)") (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 173, whole section
#ASSERT `s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` (`Provision of the Code` OF 286.3, "") (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last listed
#ASSERT `s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` (`Provision of the Code` OF 150, "") (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` (`Provision of the Code` OF 286.4, "") (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` (`Provision of the Code` OF 151, "") (`s 486 test: a witness`) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the text names the prosecutor or the accused as applicant
#ASSERT `s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` (`Provision of the Code` OF 151, "") (`s 486 test: the court on its own motion`) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` (`Provision of the Code` OF 151, "") (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an order was made: "if no such order is made"

§ `s 486(4) -- no adverse inference`
#ASSERT `s 486(4) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no adverse inference may be drawn from that fact
#ASSERT `s 486(4) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an inference from some other fact: the subsection is silent

§ `s 486.1(1) -- support person or animal for a witness under 18 or with a disability`
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) 17 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- under 18
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted` (`s 486 test: a witness`) 17 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- on application of the witness
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) 18 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- 18 is not "under the age of 18 years"
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) 18 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a mental or physical disability
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted` (`s 486 test: the court on its own motion`) 17 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted` (`s 486 test: the accused`) 17 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) 17 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- unless the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice

§ `s 486.1(1.1) -- victims of the listed offences`
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1.1) the proceedings are in respect of one of the offences the subsection names` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1.1) the proceedings are in respect of one of the offences the subsection names` FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1.1) the proceedings are in respect of one of the offences the subsection names` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence against their intimate partner
#ASSERT NOT (`s 486.1(1.1) the proceedings are in respect of one of the offences the subsection names` FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 486.1(1.1) the proceedings are in respect of one of the offences the subsection names` FALSE FALSE NOTHING)   -- s 2 "intimate partner" not answered: not shown
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1.1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for a victim` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1.1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for a victim` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (`s 486 test: a witness`) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1.1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for a victim` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not one of the named offences
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1.1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for a victim` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the witness is not a victim
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1.1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for a victim` TRUE NOTHING (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 2 "victim" not answered
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1.1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for a victim` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (`s 486 test: the court on its own motion`) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1.1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for a victim` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- unless the order would interfere

§ `s 486.1(1.2) -- inquiry by the court`
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1.2) the judge or justice must inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps have been taken to inform the witness that an application may be made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no application was made: the judge or justice inquires of the prosecutor
#ASSERT `s 486.1(1.2) the judge or justice must inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps have been taken to inform the witness that an application may be made` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an application was made: the duty to inquire does not arise

§ `s 486.1(2) -- other witnesses`
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2) the judge or justice may order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for another witness` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2) the judge or justice may order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for another witness` (`s 486 test: a witness`) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2) the judge or justice may order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for another witness` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no opinion: a failed "if" gate on a power
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2) the judge or justice may order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for another witness` (`s 486 test: the court on its own motion`) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not on their own motion: the text names an application
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2) the judge or justice may order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for another witness` (`s 486 test: the accused`) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 486.1(2.1), (3)`
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- during the proceedings, to the presiding judge or justice
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- during the proceedings the text names only the presiding judge or justice
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- that judge or justice has not been determined
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the judge who will preside has not been determined: any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the judge who will preside has been determined: the grant is limited to that judge
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- before the proceedings begin the text does not name the presiding judge
#ASSERT `s 486.1(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` `s 486(1.1) another judge or justice` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another judge
#ASSERT `s 486.1(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.1(3)(a) the age of the witness`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.1(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.1(3)(b) the witness’ mental or physical disabilities, if any`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.1(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.1(3)(c) the nature of the offence`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.1(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.1(3)(d) the nature of any relationship between the witness and the accused`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.1(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.1(3)(e) whether the witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.1(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.1(3)(f) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (f) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.1(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.1(3)(g) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (g): any other factor the judge or justice considers relevant
#ASSERT `s 486.1(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.1(3)(g) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (g): a factor the judge or justice does not consider relevant
#ASSERT `s 486.1(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.1(3)(a) the age of the witness`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- outside the determination the lead-in names

§ `s 486.1(4) to (7)`
#ASSERT `s 486.1(4) the judge or justice is barred from permitting a witness to be a support person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a witness as support person, no opinion of necessity: barred
#ASSERT `s 486.1(4) the judge or justice is barred from permitting a witness to be a support person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless ... necessary for the proper administration of justice"
#ASSERT `s 486.1(4) the judge or justice is barred from permitting a witness to be a support person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a witness
#ASSERT `s 486.1(5) the judge or justice may order that the support person and the witness not communicate with each other while the witness testifies` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.1(5) the judge or justice may order that the support person and the witness not communicate with each other while the witness testifies` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486.1(5) the judge or justice may order that the support person and the witness not communicate with each other while the witness testifies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486.1(6) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no adverse inference may be drawn from that fact
#ASSERT `s 486.1(6) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an inference from some other fact: the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 486.1(7) the judge or justice must include the reasons for their decision, in writing, in the record` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no order made: reasons in writing in the record
#ASSERT `s 486.1(7) the judge or justice must include the reasons for their decision, in writing, in the record` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an order was made: the duty does not arise

§ `s 486.2(1) -- testimony outside the court room or behind a screen`
#ASSERT `s 486.2(1) the judge or justice must order that the witness testify outside the court room or behind a screen, at the option of the witness` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) 17 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.2(1) the judge or justice must order that the witness testify outside the court room or behind a screen, at the option of the witness` (`s 486 test: a witness`) 30 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- able to communicate evidence but may have difficulty by reason of a disability
#ASSERT `s 486.2(1) the judge or justice must order that the witness testify outside the court room or behind a screen, at the option of the witness` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) 18 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486.2(1) the judge or justice must order that the witness testify outside the court room or behind a screen, at the option of the witness` (`s 486 test: the court on its own motion`) 17 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.2(1) the judge or justice must order that the witness testify outside the court room or behind a screen, at the option of the witness` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) 17 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- unless the order would interfere
