#ASSERT `s 486.2(1.2) the judge or justice must inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps have been taken to inform the witness that an application may be made` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an application was made: the duty to inquire does not arise
#ASSERT `s 486.2(2) the judge or justice may order that another witness testify outside the court room or behind a screen, at the option of the witness` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.2(2) the judge or justice may order that another witness testify outside the court room or behind a screen, at the option of the witness` (`s 486 test: a witness`) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.2(2) the judge or justice may order that another witness testify outside the court room or behind a screen, at the option of the witness` (`s 486 test: a witness`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486.2(2) the judge or justice may order that another witness testify outside the court room or behind a screen, at the option of the witness` (`s 486 test: the court on its own motion`) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486.2(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- during the proceedings, to the presiding judge or justice
#ASSERT `s 486.2(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- during the proceedings the text names only the presiding judge or justice
#ASSERT `s 486.2(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside
#ASSERT `s 486.2(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- that judge or justice has not been determined
#ASSERT `s 486.2(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the judge who will preside has not been determined: any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district
#ASSERT `s 486.2(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the judge who will preside has been determined: the grant is limited to that judge
#ASSERT `s 486.2(2.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- before the proceedings begin the text does not name the presiding judge
