#ASSERT `s 486.2(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.2(3)(f.1) whether the order is needed to protect the witness’s identity if they have had, have or will have responsibilities relating to national security or intelligence`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (f.1) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.2(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.2(3)(g) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (g) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.2(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.2(3)(h) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (h): any other factor the judge or justice considers relevant
#ASSERT `s 486.2(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.2(3)(h) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (h): a factor the judge or justice does not consider relevant
#ASSERT `s 486.2(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.2(3)(a) the age of the witness`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- outside the determination the lead-in names
#ASSERT `s 486.2(4) the judge or justice must order that the witness testify in accordance with subsection (2)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.2(4) the judge or justice must order that the witness testify in accordance with subsection (2)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5) the bar on testifying outside the court room unless the accused, the judge or justice and the jury can watch by closed-circuit television or videoconference and the accused may communicate with counsel
#ASSERT `s 486.2(5) the witness is barred from testifying outside the court room in accordance with the order` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.2(5) the witness is barred from testifying outside the court room in accordance with the order` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- they can watch but the accused cannot communicate with counsel
#ASSERT `s 486.2(5) the witness is barred from testifying outside the court room in accordance with the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the accused can communicate but no arrangement to watch
#ASSERT `s 486.2(5) the witness is barred from testifying outside the court room in accordance with the order` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- both conditions met: "unless"
#ASSERT `s 486.2(5) the witness is barred from testifying outside the court room in accordance with the order` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- behind a screen, not outside the court room: the subsection does not speak to it
#ASSERT `s 486.2(6) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no adverse inference may be drawn from that fact
#ASSERT `s 486.2(6) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an inference from some other fact: the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 486.2(7) the judge or justice must include the reasons for their decision, in writing, in the record` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no order made: reasons in writing in the record
#ASSERT `s 486.2(7) the judge or justice must include the reasons for their decision, in writing, in the record` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an order was made: the duty does not arise

§ `s 486.3 -- the accused not to cross-examine`
#ASSERT `s 486.3(1) the judge or justice must order that the accused not personally cross-examine the witness under 18` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) 17 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(1) the judge or justice must order that the accused not personally cross-examine the witness under 18` (`s 486 test: a witness`) 17 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(1) the judge or justice must order that the accused not personally cross-examine the witness under 18` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) 18 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- 18 is not under 18
#ASSERT `s 486.3(1) the judge or justice must order that the accused not personally cross-examine the witness under 18` (`s 486 test: the accused`) 17 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the accused is not an applicant named here
#ASSERT `s 486.3(1) the judge or justice must order that the accused not personally cross-examine the witness under 18` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) 17 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- unless the proper administration of justice requires the accused to cross-examine
#ASSERT `s 486.3(1) the judge or justice must appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(1) the judge or justice must appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(2) the judge or justice must order that the accused not personally cross-examine the victim` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(2) the judge or justice must order that the accused not personally cross-examine the victim` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486.3(2) the judge or justice must order that the accused not personally cross-examine the victim` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (`s 486 test: the court on its own motion`) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(2) the judge or justice must order that the accused not personally cross-examine the victim` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(2) the judge or justice must appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(2) the judge or justice must appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(2.1) the judge or justice must inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps have been taken to inform the witness that an application may be made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no application was made: the judge or justice inquires of the prosecutor
#ASSERT `s 486.3(2.1) the judge or justice must inquire of the prosecutor whether reasonable steps have been taken to inform the witness that an application may be made` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an application was made: the duty to inquire does not arise
-- (3) other witnesses: the witness must not be entitled to apply under (1) or (2)
#ASSERT `s 486.3(3) the judge or justice may order that the accused not personally cross-examine another witness` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(3) the judge or justice may order that the accused not personally cross-examine another witness` (`s 486 test: a witness`) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(3) the judge or justice may order that the accused not personally cross-examine another witness` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the witness is entitled to apply under (1) or (2)
#ASSERT `s 486.3(3) the judge or justice may order that the accused not personally cross-examine another witness` (`s 486 test: the accused`) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486.3(3) the judge or justice may order that the accused not personally cross-examine another witness` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no opinion
#ASSERT `s 486.3(3) the judge or justice must appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(3) the judge or justice must appoint counsel to conduct the cross-examination` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.3(4)(a) the age of the witness`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.3(4)(b) the witness’ mental or physical disabilities, if any`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.3(4)(c) the nature of the offence`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.3(4)(d) whether the witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.3(4)(e) the nature of any relationship between the witness and the accused`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.3(4)(f) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (f) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.3(4)(g) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (g): any other factor the judge or justice considers relevant
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.3(4)(g) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (g): a factor the judge or justice does not consider relevant
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.3(4)(a) the age of the witness`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- outside the determination the lead-in names
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- during the proceedings, to the presiding judge or justice
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- during the proceedings the text names only the presiding judge or justice
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- before the proceedings begin, to the judge or justice who will preside
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) the judge or justice who will preside at the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- that judge or justice has not been determined
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the judge who will preside has not been determined: any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) any judge or justice having jurisdiction in the judicial district where the proceedings will take place` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the judge who will preside has been determined: the grant is limited to that judge
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) before the proceedings begin` `s 486(1.1) the presiding judge or justice` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- before the proceedings begin the text does not name the presiding judge
#ASSERT `s 486.3(4.1) the application may be made to the judge or justice` `s 486(1.1) during the proceedings` `s 486(1.1) another judge or justice` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another judge
#ASSERT `s 486.3(5) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that counsel is, or is not, appointed under this section` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no adverse inference may be drawn from that fact
#ASSERT `s 486.3(5) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that counsel is, or is not, appointed under this section` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an inference from some other fact: the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 486.3(6) the judge or justice must include the reasons for their decision, in writing, in the record` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no order made: reasons in writing in the record
#ASSERT `s 486.3(6) the judge or justice must include the reasons for their decision, in writing, in the record` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an order was made: the duty does not arise

§ `s 486.31 -- non-disclosure of a witness's identity`
#ASSERT `s 486.31(1) the judge or justice may order that information that could identify the witness not be disclosed in the course of the proceedings` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.31(1) the judge or justice may order that information that could identify the witness not be disclosed in the course of the proceedings` (`s 486 test: a witness`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.31(1) the judge or justice may order that information that could identify the witness not be disclosed in the course of the proceedings` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 486.31(1) the judge or justice may order that information that could identify the witness not be disclosed in the course of the proceedings` (`s 486 test: the court on its own motion`) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not on their own motion
#ASSERT `s 486.31(1) the judge or justice may order that information that could identify the witness not be disclosed in the course of the proceedings` (`s 486 test: the accused`) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
