#ASSERT `s 486.31(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.31(3)(b) the nature of the offence`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.31(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.31(3)(c) whether the witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.31(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.31(3)(d) whether the order is needed to protect the security of anyone known to the witness`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.31(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.31(3)(e) whether the order is needed to protect the identity of a peace officer who has acted, is acting or will be acting in an undercover capacity, or of a person who has acted, is acting or will be acting covertly under the direction of a peace officer`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.31(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.31(3)(e.1) whether the order is needed to protect the witness’s identity if they have had, have or will have responsibilities relating to national security or intelligence`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e.1) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.31(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.31(3)(f) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (f) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.31(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.31(3)(g) the importance of the witness’ testimony to the case`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (g) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.31(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.31(3)(h) whether effective alternatives to the making of the proposed order are available in the circumstances`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (h) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.31(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.31(3)(i) the salutary and deleterious effects of the proposed order`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (i) is listed: always to be considered
#ASSERT `s 486.31(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.31(3)(j) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (j): any other factor the judge or justice considers relevant
#ASSERT `s 486.31(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.31(3)(j) any other factor that the judge or justice considers relevant`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (j): a factor the judge or justice does not consider relevant
#ASSERT `s 486.31(3) the judge or justice must consider the factor` (`s 486.31(3)(a) the right to a fair and public hearing`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- outside the determination the lead-in names
#ASSERT `s 486.31(4) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no adverse inference may be drawn from that fact
#ASSERT `s 486.31(4) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an inference from some other fact: the subsection is silent

§ `s 486.7 and s 486.71 -- security of witnesses`
#ASSERT `s 486.7(1) the presiding judge or justice may make an order to protect the security of a witness` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.7(1) the presiding judge or justice may make an order to protect the security of a witness` (`s 486 test: a witness`) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 486.7(1) the presiding judge or justice may make an order to protect the security of a witness` (`s 486 test: the court on its own motion`) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- on their own motion
#ASSERT `s 486.7(1) the presiding judge or justice may make an order to protect the security of a witness` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "other than one that may be made under any of sections 486 to 486.5"
#ASSERT `s 486.7(1) the presiding judge or justice may make an order to protect the security of a witness` (`s 486 test: the prosecutor`) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- necessary to protect security, but not otherwise in the interest of the proper administration of justice
